# agentmemory ingestion manifest — describes which in-repo docs to
# ingest into agentmemory's memory store. Processed by
# `scripts/import-repo-docs.sh` (typically called from the Stop hook).
#
# Format: gitignore-style. One glob per line. `!` prefix excludes.
# `#` is a comment. Excludes win over includes. Globs are relative to
# the repo root. `**` is supported.
#
# V2 behavior:
#   - Files larger than AGENTMEMORY_DOC_MAX_BYTES (default 50KB) get
#     split by ## / ### / paragraph boundaries with greedy coalescing,
#     so big runbooks land as multiple memories instead of being skipped.
#   - Filenames matching `**/session-handoff-YYYY-MM-DD*.md` are routed
#     as `[Session handoff]` memories tagged with `session:<id>` concepts
#     for every session on that date for this project.
#   - Sidecar is keyed by <project-basename>:<rel-path>, so repo moves
#     don't trigger phantom re-imports.
#
# This file is itself an example you can copy to other repos.

# Top-level README + design docs.
README.md

# When deploy/ docs stabilize, ingest them so the patterns are
# searchable across sessions. For now there's no upstream design doc
# directory worth ingesting here (the upstream README.md covers it).

# Skip transient files. (Note: if you want session-handoff-*.md ingested
# WITH session-linking, REMOVE the matching exclude — V2 handles them
# specially. We exclude them here in the agentmemory repo only because
# this repo's plans/ subdir isn't yet populated.)
!docs/plans/session-handoff-*.md
!docs/external-review-*.md
